  data: {
    LLM: "Balance between playing cards to tricks and keeping cards for melds. Ideally, play low cards to tricks while keeping meldable combinations in hand. Win tricks when you need to declare melds.\n\nThe tension between capturing Aces/Tens in tricks vs. using them in melds. Sometimes discard a high card early to develop a meld. The Marjolet (trump Jack) is extremely valuable - it can be melded multiple times with different Queens.\n\nMemory is essential - track which cards have been played to know what melds are possible. Decide when to 'close' by drawing the last stock card based on your hand strength. In the final 6 tricks, carefully manage your cards to follow the stricter rules.",
